    <h2 id="time-to-think_2995916624271">Time to Think</h2>
    <p>As you work through the course, you will be presented with a number of Time to Think boxes. Please watch this video which will show you how to use these and why they are important.</p>

    <!-- all.njk VIDEO 2 -->
    
    
      <div class="l-video-container">
        <video poster="~/images/svg/poster.svg" controls preload="metadata" aria-labelledby="time-to-think_2995916624271" width="1000"
          data-base="uc-time-to-think" 
          data-ext=".mp4" 
          data-multi="false"
          data-trans="uc-time-to-think undefined">
          <source src="https://kpcontent.blob.core.windows.net/$web/resources/v2l/720/uc-time-to-think.mp4" type="video/mp4">
          <track default label="English" kind="captions" srclang="en" src="~/videos/captions/vtt/uc-time-to-think.vtt">
          <p>Sorry, your browser doesn't support embedded videos</p>
        </video>
      </div>
      
          <toggle-section open="false">
            <h3>Video transcript </h3>
            <p><strong>Lloyd:</strong> Hi. In this Time to Think video, I'm going to demonstrate the purpose of the Time to Think boxes that you will encounter throughout the course and how they can assist you when you come to complete your assessment questions.</p>
<p>So as you can see, I'm currently on page one of session one of unit one. And if I scroll down, you can see there's some useful information relating to the different topics that you will cover; the different icons that you will encounter as you work through. And by clicking on those, it will explain what each of those icons is. There are also a couple of videos relating to submitting assessments, this video -- the Time to Think. And then if I click on page two, this page contains information relating to your learning goals and some goal setting information and also some hints and tips that relate to unit one. Each of the units has their own hints and tips, which you can download from page one of each of the units. And then on page three, you then come to the actual content relating to understanding coding.</p>
<p>So as you can see, scroll down there, there are various elements. There's videos, there's things to read, sliders, there are quizzes, there are read items. And then on page four, there's further information relating to the types of language, syntax and technologies and more videos. And then, as you come to the bottom of page four, you will see there is a Time to Think box. These Time to Think boxes are designed to make you think and generate ideas that will assist you when you come to answer the assessment questions.</p>
<p>So this very first Time to Think is asking what items in your home do you think uses code to run? So what are the different devices in your home that would need to have code within them to operate? I'll just put TV in there. And if I click save, that is then being saved to my journal. So as you work through the course, each of the different sessions and each of the units, you will encounter a number of Time to Thinks and they do relate directly to the assessment questions. So, there's another Time to Think there, and if I just type in there, this one is asking that now that I've watched the video, have a think about the roles and why teamworking is important.</p>
<p>I'll just type &quot;test&quot; in there, click save, and again, the journal entry has been saved. So how do I access that? So if I go back to the top and click on My Course, and then I look at the top, I can see my Journal. If I click on my journal icon, I can see there that on the 27th, these are the entries that I've made into my journal.</p>
<p>And it's unit one, session one, page four. Unit one, session two, page two. And as you can see the information that I have typed into the Time to Think box has been saved. So when you come to do the actual questions in the assessment, you can refer back to your journal. There's a little calendar at the top there, which will have a tick next to it, which will indicate that information has been entered on that date and then you can scroll down through the information that you've saved and find that information, and hopefully that can assist you when you come to complete your assessment questions.</p>

          </toggle-section>
        
      
  
</section>

  





